":"SZhqfsybVp8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/SZhqfsybVp8","before":{"purpose":"Develop horizontal jumping power and controlled two-foot landings.","description":"Stand with both feet stable and a clear landing area. Jump forward as assigned, absorb through hips, knees and ankles, then hold balance before resetting. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push forward. Land quietly. Hold still. Avoid: Chasing distance beyond control, landing stiff-legged or falling forward after contact.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Week 1 reactive work","description":"Jump forward with two feet and hold your landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push hard. Land firm. Avoid: Do not fall forward.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY03","name":"Two-Leg Pogos","video_id":"l6kbuPq2aHU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/l6kbuPq2aHU","before":{"purpose":"Practise small, rhythmic two-foot ankle contacts.","description":"Stand tall on a suitable, non-slip training surface. Make low, continuous jumps from both feet, keeping the knees softly responsive and contacts under the body. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Small bounce. Even rhythm. Avoid: Deep squatting, rigidly straight knees or continuing when contacts become heavy or uneven.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Week 1 onward","description":"Make small, quick jumps using both feet.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stiff ankles. Quick off the ground. Avoid: Do not bend your knees too much.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY04","name":"Drop to Hold","video_id":"ZXRiDxgcJZE","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ZXRiDxgcJZE","before":{"purpose":"Practise absorbing a drop and holding a stable landing.","description":"Use only the starting height or position Coach Du assigns. Drop into the demonstrated landing, absorb through hips, knees and ankles and become still before resetting; if using a box, step off rather than jump up first. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Absorb softly. Knees follow toes. Hold balance. Avoid: Adding height, rebounding immediately or landing with rigid legs.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Weeks 2–4","description":"Drop down into a strong landing position and hold it.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land firm. Own the position. Avoid: Do not let your knees fall in.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY05","name":"Single-Leg Hop + Stick","video_id":"IEGb_26TH6Q","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/IEGb_26TH6Q","before":{"purpose":"Develop control of a single-leg hop and landing.","description":"Stand balanced on the assigned leg with a clear landing space. Hop as prescribed, absorb on that leg and hold balance before the next repetition. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push with control. Soft knee. Stick the landing. Avoid: Chasing distance, letting the knee collapse inward or hopping again before balance is regained.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Weeks 2–4","description":"Hop on one leg and hold the landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land firm. Stay balanced. Avoid: Do not let your knee fall in.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY06","name":"Forward / Backward Pogos","video_id":"_cOsAkPbA-Q","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/_cOsAkPbA-Q","before":{"purpose":"Practise rhythmic forward and backward ankle contacts.","description":"Start tall with both feet under you on a clear surface. Make small two-foot contacts forward and backward as shown, keeping the distance short and rhythm even. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small travel. Quick rhythm. Feet under body. Avoid: Large leaps, drifting out of balance or letting contacts become loud and heavy.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Reactive ankle strength and control.","description":"Make small, quick jumps forward and backward.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small jumps. Quick ground contact. Avoid: Do not jump too far.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY07","name":"Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"GE64gjOBNzU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/GE64gjOBNzU","before":{"purpose":"Practise rhythmic ankle contacts and balance on one leg.","description":"Balance on the assigned leg on a suitable training surface. Make low repeated contacts under the hip, using the other leg for balance as shown. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall body. Small bounce. Steady rhythm. Avoid: Hopping too high, letting the knee collapse inward or continuing after rhythm is lost.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Single-leg ankle strength and control.","description":"Make small, quick jumps on one leg.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Quick off the ground. Avoid: Do not let your knee fall in.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY08","name":"Jump Squat + Stick","video_id":"v20rnNpFVfE","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/v20rnNpFVfE","before":{"purpose":"Develop vertical jumping power with a controlled stop on landing.","description":"Start in a comfortable athletic stance. Dip and jump vertically, then absorb the landing and hold still before resetting for the next repetition. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push tall. Land softly. Hold balance. Avoid: Landing stiff-legged, knees collapsing inward or rushing into the next jump.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Jump power and landing control.","description":"Jump straight up, then land and hold your position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Jump tall. Land firm. Avoid: Do not let your knees fall in.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY09","name":"Repeated Vertical Jumps","video_id":"vlToXrdgJos","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/vlToXrdgJos","before":{"purpose":"Practise repeated vertical jumping with consistent alignment.","description":"Use a clear landing area and the jump rhythm Coach Du prescribes. Jump vertically, absorb each landing and move into the next jump while posture remains controlled. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push up. Land 