anding before directing the next push. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push across. Control contact. Keep rhythm. Avoid: Chasing distance, uncontrolled trunk sway or continuing when landings become unstable.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Lateral power, rhythm and control.","description":"Jump side to side from one leg to the other.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push the ground away. Avoid: Do not rush and lose balance.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"PLY12","name":"Continuous Bench-Assisted Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"FNmXU6Y0dSA","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/FNmXU6Y0dSA","before":{"purpose":"Practise continuous vertical single-leg contacts with bench assistance.","description":"Secure the bench and position the assisted leg exactly as shown. Make small vertical contacts on the working leg, keeping the support steady and rhythm even. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Bounce vertically. Light contacts. Avoid: Using a loose bench, pushing excessively through the assisted leg or letting the knee collapse inward.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":null,"description":null,"coaching_cues":"Continuous vertical contacts; stay tall and keep a steady r