","name":"Progressive 40m Build-Up","video_id":"bj8mm2fTEfU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/bj8mm2fTEfU","before":{"purpose":"Prepare for faster running by gradually increasing speed.","description":"Use a clear 40 m lane plus room to slow down. Begin relaxed and build smoothly to the assigned effort, then ease down beyond the finish. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Build smoothly. Relax shoulders. Run through. Avoid: Sprinting hard from the first step, exceeding the assigned effort or stopping suddenly.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Every-session speed transition","description":"Start relaxed and slowly increase your speed over 40 metres.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Build your speed smoothly. Avoid: Do not sprint from step one.","admin_notes":null},"review_status":"named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified"},{"code":"SPR01","name":"A-March","video_id":"4lQsMyKRRn8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/4lQsMyKRRn8","before":{"purpose":"Practise upright marching rhythm and foot placement for running.","description":"Stand tall on a clear lane. March forward with coordinated opposite arm and leg action, placing each foot under the body rather than reaching ahead. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall hips. Toes up. Step under you. Avoid: Leaning back, stamping the foot or lifting the knee by rounding the trunk.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"purpose":"Every-session sprint prep","description":"March forward with one knee up at a time.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Knee up. Step down strong. Avoid: Do not lean back